@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] cedar-role-matrix
Cedar MUST grant VM read to owner, manager, operator and viewer; write to
owner, manager and operator; and manage to owner and manager. Persisted
administrators additionally receive read/write/manage/web authority under ADR-0058.
No matching
current principal membership MUST deny access. Only the trusted compute system
principal may coordinate internal resources. See ADR-0008 and ADR-0018.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] cedar-control-room-read-only
Every current user may perform admin_read on the Marshall ControlPlane. This
permission MUST NOT grant administrative mutations, VM override, terminal or SSH
access. Administrative mutations MUST continue to require persisted administrator
membership and recent passkey elevation. See ADR-0119.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] cedar-web-only-role
The web action MUST allow owner, manager, operator, viewer, web-only grants and
current team members/admins on team machines; team use creates no per-machine grant.
Web-only grants MUST NOT allow read, write or manage; terminal and SSH authority
MUST continue to use their existing VM actions. See ADR-0047.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] cedar-schema-policy-alignment
Policy entity/action names and VM owner/web/viewer/operator/manager fields MUST
remain consistent with the Cedar schema and the entity construction in
Marshall.Access.Authorization and Marshall.Authorization.Cedar. A schema or
policy change MUST preserve their fail-closed authorization behavior.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;product] cedar-team-member-use
Current team members MUST receive VM read, write and web for team machines; only
team owners/admins receive manage through team membership. Write admits guest
SSH, personal terminal and profile-permitted agent use, including its existing
narrow prompt wake. Web admits private guest HTTP and WebSockets under the
existing current-login and bounded lease checks. These use rights MUST NOT grant ordinary lifecycle, resize, clone,
relocation or per-machine grant management. The Access boundary MUST retain
Customer owner-only access before applying Cedar. See ADR-0077 and ADR-0110.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] cedar-service-principals
Library services MUST be distinct principals from users and the compute system:
Service::"ash_authentication" may only authenticate and Service::"scim" may only
scim_provision, each on Internal entities named by a resource's `cedar` service
mapping, and SCIM only while its `enabled` attribute is true. Neither service
may coordinate, provision or act on user-owned entities. See ADR-0268.
